response:
**Gates before launch**

I run this same script twice in cheaper modes before the full launch. The first run uses `mode: 'gates'`. It checks that grade.py scores the oracle labels at 100% and scores empty and wrong labels at 0%. It regrades round 3's saved outputs and requires them to match round 3's logged numbers within 0.005. It also sends the Opus judge 4 synthetic replies with known tone mixed with 20 round 3 replies, shuffled and blind. All 4 synthetic verdicts must be right, and the judge must agree with round 3's verdicts at least 80% of the time. The second run uses `mode: 'dry'` on 3 cells: B on ticket 1, and C2 on tickets 1 and 2. It proves the whole chain works end to end: runner, peek scan, grader, judge, failure analysis, and critic. It also gives a measured cost per trial. I set `estTrialUsd` from that measurement and pass the gate and dry spend in as `priorSpendUsd`. Only then do I launch `mode: 'full'` with `gatesPassed: true` and `dryRunPassed: true`. If any gate fails, I halt and report to you instead of launching. I commit the script as `SPE r04 evaluate (harness)` before the first launch.

**spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js**

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-eval-b-vs-c2',
  description: 'SPE eval round comparing config B (12-line prompt, 6 tools) with config C2 (12-line prompt, 3 tools plus check_status) on 50 tickets. Code grader first, Opus tone judge second, spend cap enforced. Modes: gates, dry, full. The round number lives in the ROUND constant.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Gates' },
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Peek scan' },
    { title: 'Code grade' },
    { title: 'Tone judge' },
    { title: 'Split cells' },
    { title: 'Failure analysis' },
    { title: 'Completeness' },
  ],
};

// Assumptions. Confirm them against the round 3 script before the gates run.
// 1. Trials go through the same trial runner that round 3 used. The model under test runs inside
//    that runner with only the config's prompt and tools. The runner writes one result JSON and one
//    transcript per ticket and records the measured API cost in USD.
// 2. grade.py grades a run directory against answers.json and prints per-ticket results.
// 3. The script cannot measure what its own agents cost. Those costs are estimates passed in args.
// 4. The script cannot write files. The main session saves the returned object as the results file.

const ROUND = 4;
const pad2 = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');
const R = `r${pad2(ROUND)}`;
const PREV = `r${pad2(ROUND - 1)}`;

const A = typeof args === 'object' && args !== null ? args : {};
const MODE = A.mode ?? 'gates'; // 'gates' | 'dry' | 'full'
if (!['gates', 'dry', 'full'].includes(MODE)) throw new Error(`Unknown mode ${MODE}. Use gates, dry, or full.`);

const CONFIGS = {
  B: '12-line prompt, 6 tools',
  C2: '12-line prompt, 3 tools plus a separate check_status tool',
};
const CFG_IDS = Object.keys(CONFIGS);
const TICKET_COUNT = 50;
const TRIALS_PER_CELL = 5;
const EXTRA_TRIALS_PER_SPLIT_CELL = 5;
const MAX_SPLIT_CELLS = 30;
const JUDGE_BATCH = 10;
const CAP_USD = 40;
const REGRADE_TOLERANCE = 0.005;
const JUDGE_CONTROL_SAMPLE = 20;
const JUDGE_CONTROL_MIN_AGREEMENT = 0.8;
const FAILURE_LIST_MAX = 200;

const AGENT_MODEL = A.agentModel ?? 'opus';
const JUDGE_MODEL = 'opus';

const P = {
  answers: 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json',
  tasks: 'spe/evals/tasks/',
  grader: 'spe/evals/graders/grade.py',
  judge: 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md',
  prevScript: `spe/evals/harness/${PREV}-workflow.js`,
  runs: MODE === 'dry' ? `spe/evals/runs/${R}-dry` : `spe/evals/runs/${R}`,
  results: `spe/evals/results/${R}${MODE === 'dry' ? '-dry' : ''}.json`,
  failures: 'spe/failures.md',
  predictionLog: 'spe/prediction-log.md',
};

// A trial transcript that contains any of these strings is voided.
const FORBIDDEN = ['answers.json', 'grade.py', 'judge.md', 'spe/evals/graders', 'spe/predictions', 'prediction-log', 'spe/plans/'];
const NO_PEEK = `Do not open, list, grep, or print anything under spe/evals/graders/, spe/predictions/, or spe/plans/. Do not open ${P.answers} or ${P.predictionLog}.`;

const RUNNER = A.runnerCmd
  ? `Use this runner command: ${A.runnerCmd}`
  : `Use the same trial runner command that ${P.prevScript} uses. Change only the round (set it to ${R}), the config, the trial number, the ticket selection, and the output directory.`;

// Cost estimates. Dry and gates runs use 1 USD per call as a deliberately high bound. That is not a measurement.
const DRY_DEFAULT_USD = 1;
const EST = {
  estTrialUsd: A.estTrialUsd ?? (MODE === 'full' ? null : DRY_DEFAULT_USD),
  estAgentUsd: A.estAgentUsd ?? (MODE === 'full' ? null : DRY_DEFAULT_USD),
  estJudgeBatchUsd: A.estJudgeBatchUsd ?? (MODE === 'full' ? null : DRY_DEFAULT_USD),
};
if (MODE === 'full') {
  if (A.gatesPassed !== true || A.dryRunPassed !== true) {
    throw new Error('Run mode "gates" and mode "dry" first. Then pass gatesPassed: true and dryRunPassed: true.');
  }
  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(EST)) {
    if (!(typeof v === 'number' && v > 0)) throw new Error(`Full mode needs a positive number for args.${k}. Take it from the dry run.`);
  }
}

// ---------- schemas ----------
const S = { type: 'string' };
const N = { type: 'number' };
const I = { type: 'integer' };
const BOOL = { type: 'boolean' };
const arr = (items) => ({ type: 'array', items });
const obj = (properties) => ({ type: 'object', properties, required: Object.keys(properties), additionalProperties: false });

const SELFTEST = obj({ oracle_pass_rate: N, empty_pass_rate: N, wrong_pass_rate: N, commands: arr(S), notes: S });
const CONTROL = obj({
  recorded_source: S,
  rows: arr(obj({ config: S, metric: S, recorded: N, regraded: N })),
  judge_sample: arr(obj({ ticket: S, reply: S, recorded_tone_pass: BOOL })),
  notes: S,
});
const TRIAL = obj({
  out_dir: S,
  results: arr(obj({
    ticket: S,
    status: { type: 'string', enum: ['ok', 'error', 'cap'] },
    usd: N,
    result_file: S,
    transcript_file: S,
    error: S,
  })),
  notes: S,
});
const SCAN = obj({ command: S, files_scanned: I, hits: arr(obj({ transcript_file: S, pattern: S, excerpt: S })) });
const GRADE = obj({
  command: S,
  totals: obj({ n: I, category_correct: I, priority_correct: I }),
  rows: arr(obj({ ticket: S, category_ok: BOOL, priority_ok: BOOL, reply: S })),
  errors: arr(obj({ ticket: S, error: S })),
});
const JUDGE = obj({ verdicts: arr(obj({ id: S, tone_pass: BOOL, score: I, reason: S })) });
const FAILS = obj({
  failure_types: arr(obj({
    id: S, is_new: BOOL, name: S, kind: S, what: S, how_to_spot: S, seen_in: arr(S), count: I, fix: S,
  })),
  notes: S,
});
const CRITIC = obj({
  complete: BOOL,
  gaps: arr(obj({ what: S, severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocker', 'major', 'minor'] }, fix: S })),
});

// ---------- state, budget, halt ----------
const state = {
  rows: [],
  voids: [],
  errors: [],
  issues: [],
  okTrials: 0,
  ticketsSeen: Object.fromEntries(CFG_IDS.map((c) => [c, new Set()])),
  expectTickets: {},
};
const ledger = { prior: Number(A.priorSpendUsd) || 0, measured: 0, estimated: 0, reserved: 0, held: 0, skips: [] };
const halt = { on: false, reasons: [] };

const spent = () => ledger.prior + ledger.measured + ledger.estimated;
const hold = (usd) => { ledger.held = usd; };

function stop(reason) {
  if (!halt.reasons.includes(reason)) halt.reasons.push(reason);
  halt.on = true;
  log(`HALT: ${reason}`);
}

function reserve(usd, what) {
  if (spent() + ledger.reserved + ledger.held + usd > CAP_USD) {
    ledger.skips.push({ what, reason: 'cap', est_usd: usd, counted_usd: +spent().toFixed(2) });
    log(`Skipped (cap): ${what}. Counted ${spent().toFixed(2)}, reserved ${ledger.reserved.toFixed(2)}, held ${ledger.held.toFixed(2)}, estimate ${usd.toFixed(2)}. Cap is ${CAP_USD} USD.`);
    return false;
  }
  ledger.reserved += usd;
  return true;
}

function settle(reservedUsd, measuredUsd, estimatedUsd) {
  ledger.reserved -= reservedUsd;
  ledger.measured += measuredUsd;
  ledger.estimated += estimatedUsd;
  if (spent() > CAP_USD) stop(`Counted spend ${spent().toFixed(2)} USD is over the ${CAP_USD} USD cap.`);
}

async function paidAgent(what, est, prompt, opts, allowWhenHalted = false) {
  if (halt.on && !allowWhenHalted) {
    ledger.skips.push({ what, reason: 'halted' });
    return null;
  }
  if (!reserve(est, what)) return null;
  try {
    return await agent(prompt, opts);
  } catch (e) {
    state.issues.push(`${what}: agent failed: ${e?.message ?? e}`);
    return null;
  } finally {
    settle(est, 0, est);
  }
}

const spendRecord = () => ({
  cap_usd: CAP_USD,
  prior_usd: ledger.prior,
  measured_runner_usd: +ledger.measured.toFixed(2),
  estimated_agent_usd: +ledger.estimated.toFixed(2),
  counted_usd: +spent().toFixed(2),
  note: 'Runner cost is measured. Workflow agent cost is an estimate from args.',
});

// ---------- helpers ----------
function rng(seed) {
  let s = seed >>> 0;
  return () => {
    s = (s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;
    let t = s;
    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);
    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);
    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
  };
}
function shuffle(list, seed) {
  const r = rng(seed);
  const a = list.slice();
  for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
    const j = Math.floor(r() * (i + 1));
    [a[i], a[j]] = [a[j], a[i]];
  }
  return a;
}
function chunk(list, n) {
  const out = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i += n) out.push(list.slice(i, i + n));
  return out;
}
const ticketCount = (sel) => (sel === 'all' ? TICKET_COUNT : sel.first ? sel.first : sel.length);
function ticketText(sel) {
  if (sel === 'all') return `all ${TICKET_COUNT} tickets`;
  if (sel.first) return `only the first ${sel.first} ticket(s) in the runner's default order`;
  return `only these tickets: ${sel.join(', ')}`;
}
const rate = (rows, f) => (rows.length ? +(rows.filter(f).length / rows.length).toFixed(3) : null);

// ---------- stage 1: run trials through the runner ----------
async function runStage(b) {
  const n = ticketCount(b.tickets);
  const what = `${b.cfg} trial ${b.trial}, ${n} ticket(s)`;
  if (halt.on) {
    ledger.skips.push({ what, reason: 'halted' });
    return null;
  }
  const trialEst = n * EST.estTrialUsd;
  const est = trialEst + EST.estAgentUsd;
  if (!reserve(est, what)) return null;
  const room = Math.max(0, CAP_USD - spent() - ledger.held - (ledger.reserved - trialEst));
  const outDir = `${P.runs}/${b.cfg}/t${b.trial}`;

  let res = null;
  try {
    res = await agent(
      `You operate the trial runner for SPE round ${R}. You are not the model under test. Do not answer any ticket yourself.

Config ${b.cfg}: ${CONFIGS[b.cfg]}.
Trial number: ${b.trial}.
Tickets: ${ticketText(b.tickets)}.
Output directory: ${outDir}

${RUNNER}

Rules:
- ${NO_PEEK}
- Check the runner's measured cost as it goes. If the measured cost of this batch reaches ${room.toFixed(2)} USD, start no more tickets. Mark every ticket you did not start with status "cap".
- If the runner fails on a ticket, retry it once. If it fails again, mark it "error" and copy the runner's error text.
- Do not edit result files or transcripts.

Return one entry per ticket. Give the result file path, the transcript file path, and the measured USD for that ticket from the runner's own cost record. Use 0 for usd only when the runner did not start the ticket. Use an empty string for error when there was none.`,
      { label: `run ${b.cfg} t${b.trial}`, phase: b.extra ? 'Split cells' : 'Trials', schema: TRIAL, model: AGENT_MODEL },
    );
  } catch (e) {
    state.issues.push(`${what}: runner agent failed: ${e?.message ?? e}`);
  }

  const results = res?.results ?? [];
  const measured = results.reduce((s, r) => s + (Number(r.usd) || 0), 0);
  settle(est, measured, EST.estAgentUsd);
  if (res && results.length !== n) state.issues.push(`${what}: expected ${n} results, got ${results.length}.`);
  for (const r of results) {
    state.ticketsSeen[b.cfg].add(r.ticket);
    if (r.status === 'ok') state.okTrials++;
    if (r.status === 'cap') ledger.skips.push({ what: `${b.cfg} t${b.trial} ${r.ticket}`, reason: 'cap inside batch' });
    if (r.status === 'error') state.errors.push({ cfg: b.cfg, trial: b.trial, ticket: r.ticket, error: r.error });
  }
  return res ? { ...b, outDir, results } : null;
}

// ---------- stage 2: peek scan (code check) ----------
async function scanStage(b) {
  if (!b) return null;
  const ok = b.results.filter((r) => r.status === 'ok');
  const voided = new Set();
  if (!ok.length) return { ...b, ok, voided };

  const files = ok.map((r) => r.transcript_file);
  const cmd = `grep -n -F ${FORBIDDEN.map((p) => `-e '${p}'`).join(' ')} ${files.map((f) => `'${f}'`).join(' ')}`;
  const scan = await paidAgent(
    `peek scan ${b.cfg} t${b.trial}`,
    EST.estAgentUsd,
    `You check trial transcripts for peeking. This is a code check. Use grep, not judgment.

Run this exact command and report every matching line:
${cmd}

Do not open the files that the patterns name. Report each hit with its transcript file, the pattern it matched, and the matched line cut to 200 characters. If grep finds nothing, return an empty hits list. files_scanned is the number of transcript files in the command (${files.length}).`,
    { label: `scan ${b.cfg} t${b.trial}`, phase: 'Peek scan', schema: SCAN, model: AGENT_MODEL },
  );

  if (!scan || scan.files_scanned !== files.length) {
    for (const r of ok) {
      voided.add(r.ticket);
      state.voids.push({ cfg: b.cfg, trial: b.trial, ticket: r.ticket, reason: 'not scanned' });
    }
    return { ...b, ok, voided };
  }
  const byFile = new Map(ok.map((r) => [r.transcript_file, r.ticket]));
  for (const h of scan.hits) {
    const ticket = byFile.get(h.transcript_file) ?? `unknown (${h.transcript_file})`;
    if (!voided.has(ticket)) {
      voided.add(ticket);
      state.voids.push({ cfg: b.cfg, trial: b.trial, ticket, reason: `matched ${h.pattern}`, excerpt: h.excerpt });
    }
    if (h.pattern === 'answers.json') stop(`${b.cfg} t${b.trial} ${ticket} touched the answer key. Excerpt: ${h.excerpt}`);
  }
  return { ...b, ok, voided };
}

// ---------- stage 3: code grade ----------
async function gradeStage(b) {
  if (!b) return null;
  const keep = b.ok.filter((r) => !b.voided.has(r.ticket));
  if (!keep.length) return b;
  const tickets = keep.map((r) => r.ticket);

  const g = await paidAgent(
    `grade ${b.cfg} t${b.trial}`,
    EST.estAgentUsd,
    `You run the code grader for SPE round ${R}. Copy its output. Do not grade anything yourself.

1. Run ${P.grader} on ${b.outDir} against ${P.answers}. If you do not know its arguments, run it with --help first.
2. Keep only these tickets: ${tickets.join(', ')}.
3. For each kept ticket, copy category_ok and priority_ok exactly as grade.py printed them.
4. For each kept ticket, print the reply field of its result file with a command such as jq. Copy the reply text exactly.
5. totals counts only the kept tickets: n, category_correct, priority_correct.

If grade.py errors on a ticket, list it under errors with the error text and leave it out of rows. Do not edit any file.`,
    { label: `grade ${b.cfg} t${b.trial}`, phase: 'Code grade', schema: GRADE, model: AGENT_MODEL },
  );
  if (!g) {
    state.issues.push(`${b.cfg} t${b.trial}: not graded.`);
    return b;
  }

  const tFile = new Map(keep.map((r) => [r.ticket, r.transcript_file]));
  const rows = g.rows
    .filter((r) => tFile.has(r.ticket))
    .map((r) => ({
      cfg: b.cfg,
      trial: b.trial,
      extra: b.trial > TRIALS_PER_CELL,
      ticket: r.ticket,
      category_ok: r.category_ok,
      priority_ok: r.priority_ok,
      reply: r.reply,
      tone_pass: null,
      tone_score: null,
      tone_reason: null,
      pass: null,
      transcript: tFile.get(r.ticket),
    }));
  const cat = rows.filter((r) => r.category_ok).length;
  const pri = rows.filter((r) => r.priority_ok).length;
  if (g.totals.n !== rows.length || g.totals.category_correct !== cat || g.totals.priority_correct !== pri) {
    state.issues.push(`${b.cfg} t${b.trial}: grader totals ${JSON.stringify(g.totals)} do not match the rows (n ${rows.length}, category ${cat}, priority ${pri}).`);
  }
  const accounted = new Set([...rows.map((r) => r.ticket), ...g.errors.map((e) => e.ticket)]);
  const missing = tickets.filter((t) => !accounted.has(t));
  if (missing.length) state.issues.push(`${b.cfg} t${b.trial}: grader output is missing ${missing.join(', ')}.`);
  for (const e of g.errors) state.errors.push({ cfg: b.cfg, trial: b.trial, ticket: e.ticket, error: `grader: ${e.error}` });
  state.rows.push(...rows);
  return b;
}

// ---------- tone judge (blind, shuffled across configs) ----------
async function judgeItems(items, seed, tag) {
  const shuffled = shuffle(items, seed).map((it, i) => ({ ...it, id: `${tag}-${i + 1}` }));
  const batches = chunk(shuffled, JUDGE_BATCH);
  const out = await parallel(
    batches.map((batch, k) => async () => {
      const body = batch
        .map((it) => [
          `### ${it.id}`,
          it.ticket_text ? `Ticket text: ${it.ticket_text}` : `Ticket ID: ${it.row.ticket}`,
          'Reply:',
          it.row.reply,
        ].join('\n'))
        .join('\n\n');
      const r = await paidAgent(
        `judge ${tag} batch ${k + 1}/${batches.length}`,
        EST.estJudgeBatchUsd,
        `You judge the tone of customer support replies.

Read ${P.judge} and apply its rubric exactly. When an item gives a ticket ID, read that ticket's text from ${P.tasks}. Do not open ${P.answers}. Tone is the only thing you judge. Do not judge whether the label or the facts are right.

You are not told which system wrote each reply. Judge each one on its own.

${body}

Return one verdict per id. Give tone_pass, the rubric score, and a one-sentence reason. If the rubric has no numeric scale, use 1 for pass and 0 for fail.`,
        { label: `judge ${tag} ${k + 1}/${batches.length}`, phase: 'Tone judge', schema: JUDGE, model: JUDGE_MODEL },
      );
      return r?.verdicts ?? [];
    }),
  );
  const byId = new Map(out.flat().map((v) => [v.id, v]));
  let missing = 0;
  for (const it of shuffled) {
    const v = byId.get(it.id);
    if (!v) {
      missing++;
      continue;
    }
    it.row.tone_pass = v.tone_pass;
    it.row.tone_score = v.score;
    it.row.tone_reason = v.reason;
  }
  if (missing) state.issues.push(`judge ${tag}: ${missing} item(s) got no verdict.`);
}

const finalize = () => {
  for (const r of state.rows) r.pass = r.tone_pass === null ? null : r.category_ok && r.priority_ok && r.tone_pass;
};

function metricsFor(rows) {
  const out = {};
  for (const cfg of CFG_IDS) {
    const rs = rows.filter((r) => r.cfg === cfg);
    const judged = rs.filter((r) => r.tone_pass !== null);
    out[cfg] = {
      n_graded: rs.length,
      n_judged: judged.length,
      category_acc: rate(rs, (r) => r.category_ok),
      priority_acc: rate(rs, (r) => r.priority_ok),
      label_acc: rate(rs, (r) => r.category_ok && r.priority_ok),
      tone_pass: rate(judged, (r) => r.tone_pass),
      all_pass: rate(judged, (r) => r.pass),
    };
  }
  return out;
}

function cellTally(rows) {
  const cells = new Map();
  for (const r of rows) {
    if (r.pass === null) continue;
    const k = `${r.cfg}|${r.ticket}`;
    if (!cells.has(k)) cells.set(k, { cfg: r.cfg, ticket: r.ticket, passes: 0, n: 0 });
    const c = cells.get(k);
    c.n++;
    if (r.pass) c.passes++;
  }
  return cells;
}

function splitCells(rows) {
  const split = [...cellTally(rows).values()]
    .filter((c) => c.passes > 0 && c.passes < c.n)
    .map((c) => ({ ...c, balance: Math.abs(c.passes / c.n - 0.5) }))
    .sort((a, b) => a.balance - b.balance || `${a.cfg}|${a.ticket}`.localeCompare(`${b.cfg}|${b.ticket}`));
  if (split.length > MAX_SPLIT_CELLS) log(`${split.length} split cells found. Extra trials go to the ${MAX_SPLIT_CELLS} most balanced ones.`);
  return split.slice(0, MAX_SPLIT_CELLS);
}

function codeGaps(primaryTrials) {
  const gaps = [...state.issues];
  for (const cfg of CFG_IDS) {
    const want = state.expectTickets[cfg] ?? 0;
    const seen = state.ticketsSeen[cfg];
    if (seen.size < want) gaps.push(`${cfg}: saw ${seen.size} of ${want} tickets.`);
    for (const t of seen) {
      const n = state.rows.filter((r) => r.cfg === cfg && r.ticket === t && !r.extra && r.tone_pass !== null).length;
      if (n < primaryTrials) gaps.push(`${cfg} ${t}: ${n} of ${primaryTrials} trials graded and judged.`);
    }
  }
  return gaps;
}

// ---------- gates mode ----------
const SANITY_TICKET = 'Our nightly CSV export failed twice and I need the file for a 9am meeting tomorrow. Can someone help?';
const SANITY = [
  { expect: true, reply: 'Thanks for letting us know, and sorry about the trouble before your meeting. Both export runs failed on a timeout. I restarted the job and it finished at 10:42 PM. Could you check that the file looks right on your side?' },
  { expect: true, reply: 'Sorry for the hassle with the export. I reproduced the failure and sent it to our data team as urgent. While they fix it, I ran a manual export and attached the file here. I will update you by 8 AM tomorrow.' },
  { expect: false, reply: 'Exports fail sometimes. Try again later.' },
  { expect: false, reply: 'This is the third ticket you have opened about exports. Please read the documentation before contacting support.' },
];

async function runGates() {
  phase('Gates');
  const [self, control] = await parallel([
    () => paidAgent(
      'grader selftest',
      EST.estAgentUsd,
      `You run the grader selftest for SPE round ${R}. This is a code check.

Work in a new temporary directory outside the repo, for example one from mktemp -d. Do not write inside spe/.
Build three fake run directories in the same result file format a real trial run uses. ${P.prevScript} and round ${PREV}'s run outputs show that format.
1. oracle: every ticket's label copied from ${P.answers}.
2. empty: every ticket with an empty label.
3. wrong: every ticket's category and priority changed to a different valid value taken from ${P.answers}.
Run ${P.grader} on each one against ${P.answers}. A ticket passes only when both category and priority are correct. Report each pass rate as a number from 0 to 1. List the exact commands you ran.`,
      { label: 'grader selftest', phase: 'Gates', schema: SELFTEST, model: AGENT_MODEL },
    ),
    () => paidAgent(
      `regrade ${PREV}`,
      EST.estAgentUsd,
      `You regrade round ${PREV} as a control for round ${R}. This is a code check.

1. Find round ${PREV}'s trial outputs. ${P.prevScript} shows where it wrote them.
2. Run ${P.grader} on each round ${PREV} config's outputs against ${P.answers}.
3. Find round ${PREV}'s recorded measured category accuracy and priority accuracy in ${P.predictionLog} or in round ${PREV}'s results file. Name the source you used.
4. Report one row per config and metric with the recorded and regraded values as numbers from 0 to 1.
5. Pick ${JUDGE_CONTROL_SAMPLE} round ${PREV} replies that have a recorded tone verdict. Take half recorded passes and half recorded fails if that many exist. Take them in ticket ID order. Copy each reply text exactly, with its ticket ID and its recorded tone_pass.
Do not edit any file.`,
      { label: `regrade ${PREV} control`, phase: 'Gates', schema: CONTROL, model: AGENT_MODEL },
    ),
  ]);

  const selftestOk = !!self && self.oracle_pass_rate === 1 && self.empty_pass_rate === 0 && self.wrong_pass_rate === 0;
  const regradeOk = !!control && control.rows.length > 0 && control.rows.every((r) => Math.abs(r.recorded - r.regraded) <= REGRADE_TOLERANCE);

  const sanity = SANITY.map((s) => ({ row: { ticket: 'synthetic', reply: s.reply, tone_pass: null, expect: s.expect }, ticket_text: SANITY_TICKET }));
  const ctrl = (control?.judge_sample ?? []).map((s) => ({ row: { ticket: s.ticket, reply: s.reply, tone_pass: null, expect: s.recorded_tone_pass } }));
  await judgeItems([...sanity, ...ctrl], ROUND * 1000 + 3, 'g');

  const sanityOk = sanity.every((it) => it.row.tone_pass === it.row.expect);
  const judged = ctrl.filter((it) => it.row.tone_pass !== null);
  const agreement = judged.length ? +(judged.filter((it) => it.row.tone_pass === it.row.expect).length / judged.length).toFixed(3) : null;
  const judgeControlOk = ctrl.length > 0 && judged.length === ctrl.length && agreement >= JUDGE_CONTROL_MIN_AGREEMENT;

  const passed = selftestOk && regradeOk && sanityOk && judgeControlOk && !halt.on;
  if (!passed) log('Gates failed. Do not launch. Report to the user.');
  return {
    round: ROUND,
    mode: 'gates',
    passed,
    checks: { selftestOk, regradeOk, sanityOk, judgeControlOk, judge_control_agreement: agreement, judge_control_n: judged.length },
    selftest: self,
    control: control && { recorded_source: control.recorded_source, rows: control.rows, notes: control.notes },
    sanity: sanity.map((it) => ({ expect: it.row.expect, got: it.row.tone_pass, reason: it.row.tone_reason })),
    spend: spendRecord(),
    halt_reasons: halt.reasons,
    issues: state.issues,
  };
}

// ---------- dry and full modes ----------
async function runRound() {
  const primaryTrials = MODE === 'dry' ? 1 : TRIALS_PER_CELL;
  const primaryBatches = MODE === 'dry'
    ? [{ cfg: 'B', trial: 1, tickets: { first: 1 } }, { cfg: 'C2', trial: 1, tickets: { first: 2 } }]
    : CFG_IDS.flatMap((cfg) => Array.from({ length: TRIALS_PER_CELL }, (_, i) => ({ cfg, trial: i + 1, tickets: 'all' })));
  for (const b of primaryBatches) state.expectTickets[b.cfg] = Math.max(state.expectTickets[b.cfg] ?? 0, ticketCount(b.tickets));

  const nTrials = primaryBatches.reduce((s, b) => s + ticketCount(b.tickets), 0);
  const reportHold = 2 * EST.estAgentUsd;
  const judgeHold = Math.ceil(nTrials / JUDGE_BATCH) * EST.estJudgeBatchUsd;
  const projected = nTrials * EST.estTrialUsd + primaryBatches.length * 3 * EST.estAgentUsd + judgeHold + reportHold;
  log(`${R} ${MODE}: ${primaryBatches.length} batches, ${nTrials} trials. Projected spend ${projected.toFixed(2)} USD (estimate). Already counted ${ledger.prior.toFixed(2)} USD. Cap ${CAP_USD} USD.`);
  if (projected + ledger.prior > CAP_USD) log('The projection is over the cap. Some trials will be skipped and logged.');

  // Primary trials. Judge and report budget is held so trials cannot spend it.
  phase('Trials');
  hold(judgeHold + reportHold);
  await pipeline(primaryBatches, runStage, scanStage, gradeStage);
  hold(reportHold);

  phase('Tone judge');
  await judgeItems(state.rows.filter((r) => !r.extra).map((row) => ({ row })), ROUND * 1000 + 1, 'p');
  finalize();

  // Split cells get extra trials, full mode only.
  let split = [];
  if (MODE === 'full' && !halt.on) {
    phase('Split cells');
    split = splitCells(state.rows.filter((r) => !r.extra));
    if (split.length) {
      const extraBatches = [];
      for (let k = 1; k <= EXTRA_TRIALS_PER_SPLIT_CELL; k++) {
        for (const cfg of CFG_IDS) {
          const tickets = split.filter((c) => c.cfg === cfg).map((c) => c.ticket);
          if (tickets.length) extraBatches.push({ cfg, trial: TRIALS_PER_CELL + k, tickets, extra: true });
        }
      }
      const nExtra = extraBatches.reduce((s, b) => s + b.tickets.length, 0);
      hold(Math.ceil(nExtra / JUDGE_BATCH) * EST.estJudgeBatchUsd + reportHold);
      await pipeline(extraBatches, runStage, scanStage, gradeStage);
      hold(reportHold);
      await judgeItems(state.rows.filter((r) => r.extra && r.tone_pass === null).map((row) => ({ row })), ROUND * 1000 + 2, 'x');
      finalize();
    }
  }
  hold(0);

  const primaryRows = state.rows.filter((r) => !r.extra);
  const allTally = cellTally(state.rows);
  const splitReport = split.map((c) => {
    const after = allTally.get(`${c.cfg}|${c.ticket}`);
    return { cfg: c.cfg, ticket: c.ticket, primary: `${c.passes}/${c.n}`, with_extra: after ? `${after.passes}/${after.n}` : null };
  });

  // Failure analysis.
  phase('Failure analysis');
  const failing = state.rows.filter((r) => r.pass === false);
  const lines = failing.map((r) => {
    const why = [!r.category_ok && 'category', !r.priority_ok && 'priority', r.tone_pass === false && `tone (${r.tone_reason})`].filter(Boolean).join(', ');
    return `${r.cfg} t${r.trial} ${r.ticket}: ${why} | transcript ${r.transcript}`;
  });
  const shown = lines.slice(0, FAILURE_LIST_MAX);
  const failures = failing.length
    ? await paidAgent(
      'failure analysis',
      EST.estAgentUsd,
      `You do failure analysis for SPE round ${R}.

Configs:
${CFG_IDS.map((c) => `- ${c}: ${CONFIGS[c]}`).join('\n')}

These trials failed at least one check. Category and priority come from ${P.grader}. Tone comes from an Opus judge.
${shown.join('\n')}
${lines.length > shown.length ? `${lines.length - shown.length} more failures are not listed.` : ''}

1. Read ${P.failures} to learn the existing failure types and their F numbers.
2. Read the transcripts you need. Cover every config and every failed check type.
3. Group the failures into types. Reuse an existing F number when a failure matches it. Give a new type the next free F number and set is_new to true.
4. For each type, give the kind, what happens, how to spot it in a transcript, the trials it was seen in, the count, and a fix.
Do not read spe/predictions/ or spe/plans/. Describe what happened, not what was expected. Do not edit any file.`,
      { label: 'failure analysis', phase: 'Failure analysis', schema: FAILS, model: AGENT_MODEL },
      true,
    )
    : null;
  if (!failing.length) log('Every judged trial passed every check. The next round needs harder tasks or stricter graders.');

  // Completeness. Code checks first, then the critic.
  phase('Completeness');
  const gaps = codeGaps(primaryTrials);
  const summaryForCritic = {
    round: ROUND,
    mode: MODE,
    primary_metrics: metricsFor(primaryRows),
    metrics_with_extra_trials: metricsFor(state.rows),
    split_cells: splitReport,
    code_gaps: gaps,
    voided: state.voids,
    errors: state.errors,
    skips: ledger.skips,
    failure_types: (failures?.failure_types ?? []).map((f) => ({ id: f.id, name: f.name, count: f.count })),
    failed_trials: failing.length,
    spend: spendRecord(),
    halt_reasons: halt.reasons,
  };
  const critic = await paidAgent(
    'completeness critic',
    EST.estAgentUsd,
    `You are the completeness critic for SPE round ${R}. The run is over. Find anything missing or inconsistent that would make the close-out wrong.

Summary:
${JSON.stringify(summaryForCritic, null, 1)}

Check at least these. Every cell has ${primaryTrials} graded and judged trial(s) or a logged reason. Voided, errored, and skipped trials are all listed. Grader totals agree with the rows. The failure analysis covers every failed check type in every config. The spend record adds up. You may read run outputs under ${P.runs} to check. Do not read spe/predictions/. Do not edit any file. Do not repeat a code gap unless you add a fix.`,
    { label: 'completeness critic', phase: 'Completeness', schema: CRITIC, model: AGENT_MODEL },
    true,
  );

  const result = {
    ...summaryForCritic,
    configs: CONFIGS,
    halted: halt.on,
    failure_analysis: failures,
    critic,
    rows: state.rows.map(({ reply, ...r }) => r),
    next_steps: `Main session: save this object to ${P.results}. Commit it as "SPE ${R} evaluate (results): <headline>". Then close out in ${P.predictionLog} and ${P.failures}. Do not edit spe/predictions/${R}.yaml.`,
  };
  if (MODE === 'dry') {
    result.dry_passed = !halt.on && state.rows.length === 3 && state.rows.every((r) => r.tone_pass !== null) && !state.voids.length && !gaps.length;
    result.measured_usd_per_trial = state.okTrials ? +(ledger.measured / state.okTrials).toFixed(4) : null;
  }
  return result;
}

if (MODE === 'gates') return await runGates();
return await runRound();
